    description: "FOUND 2026-11-01 during the P4 review (batch langs1, while re-checking WI-fuzaj-...) at dev 9ae4abe13f. Fixtures: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p4_review_11012026/langs1/fx_fuzaj. For a one-letter struct name, the grammar's recovery differs by letter: for A/B/T the analyzer's single-letter recovery finds a type_placeholder and emits the struct; for C, E, F, G, S and X tree-sitter-v yields ERROR('struct S') followed by a block with no type_placeholder child, so no struct symbol is emitted. Sibling of WI-fuzaj (one-letter type alias). Same grammar mechanism: a lone capital is lexed as a type placeholder."  # 2cdd
